1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,960
How's your eyesight?
你的视力怎么样？

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:11,570
From the moment we're born, our eyes grow, our vision becomes clearer and some of us will have normal or even 20:20 vision.
从出生的那一刻起，我们的眼睛就会不断发育，视力会变得越来越清晰，有些人会拥有正常甚至是2.0的视力。

3
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:20,400
However, others will become short-sighted and end up wearing glasses or contact lenses to help them see everything clearly.
但另一些人则会患上近视，最终需要戴上眼镜或隐形眼镜才能看清事物。

4
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:28,200
And some experts claim that more of us will be wearing them in the future because of our lifestyle when we were younger.
一些专家称，由于我们年轻时的生活方式，未来会有更多人需要佩戴矫正视力的眼镜。

5
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:36,670
Even today, optometrists are reporting a rise in short-sightedness – also called myopia – in children.
即便是现在，验光师们也指出儿童患近视眼的比率正在上升。

6
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:51,290
The condition can be genetic, but it's also partly being blamed on a number of modern-day factors – particularly children staring at phone screens, computers and game consoles for long periods of time.
近视可能与遗传有关，但也有部分原因要归咎于多种现代因素——尤其是儿童长时间盯着手机屏幕、电脑和游戏机。

7
00:00:51,290 --> 00:01:04,480
It's believed myopia also makes them susceptible to secondary eye conditions such as glaucoma, retinal detachment and other visual impairments later in life.
有观点认为，近视还会让他们在日后更容易患上继发性眼部疾病，比如青光眼、视网膜脱落以及其他视力损伤问题。

8
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:16,970
Of course, children have had increased screen time due to lockdowns imposed during the Covid pandemic – it's been the only way to access education and communicate with others.
当然，新冠疫情期间的封锁措施导致儿童的屏幕使用时间有所增加——这曾是他们接受教育和与他人沟通的唯一途径。

9
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:22,040
But education generally could be blamed for the rise in myopia.
但总体而言，教育也可能是近视率上升的一个诱因。

10
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:33,410
Neema Ghorbani-Mojarrad, lecturer at the University of Bradford, told BBC Future website: "We suspect it is reading and spending more time indoors.
布拉德福德大学讲师妮玛·戈尔巴尼-莫加拉德在接受BBC未来频道采访时表示：“我们猜测原因在于阅读以及长时间待在室内。

11
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:39,220
Every year of education completed increases the expected amount of short-sightedness."
所受教育每增加一年，近视的概率就会相应上升。”

12
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:44,330
The problem appears to be more severe in some Asian countries.
这个问题在一些亚洲国家似乎更为严重。

13
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:52,970
Some experts say that in these places with huge educational success, children spend more time indoors studying.
有专家表示，在这些教育成就斐然的地区，儿童会花更多时间在室内学习。

14
00:01:52,970 --> 00:01:59,420
Therefore, it seems, spending more time outdoors could be good for children's eye health.
因此，多待在户外或许有益于儿童的眼部健康。

15
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:08,090
The UK's College of Optometrists is suggesting parents should get their kids playing outside for two hours a day.
英国验光师学院建议家长每天让孩子在户外玩耍两小时。

16
00:02:08,090 --> 00:02:14,080
Several scientific studies show this can prevent or stop the development of myopia.
多项科学研究表明，这样做能够预防或阻止近视的产生。

17
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:28,640
There's been a focus on using technology, such as laser surgery, for fixing myopia, but for children at least, it seems a dose of daylight and a break from the screen might be part of the solution.
目前人们很关注用激光手术等技术来矫正近视，但至少对于儿童来说，似乎多接触日光、远离屏幕或许应该是一部分解决方案。

18
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:38,240
Opticians also recommend kids have regular eye tests to identify any problems before they become more severe.
配镜师还建议，儿童应定期进行视力检查，以便在眼部问题恶化之前及时发现。
